.TITLE "open"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Opens files, directories, or applications using their default handlers. It mimics the behavior of double-clicking an icon in the __Finder__ and can launch URLs, applications, and documents.

.DIV "TLDR"
**open file.txt**
Opens a file with the default associated application defined by the system.
> __file.txt__ the file to open

**open -a "Application"**
Launches a specific application by its name.
> __-a__ application flag | __"Application"__ the app name

**open .**
Opens the current working directory in a new Finder window.
> __.__ current directory reference

**open -e file.txt**
Opens a specific file using the TextEdit application.
> __-e__ editor flag | __file.txt__ the file to open

**open -R file.txt**
Reveals the specified file in a Finder window instead of opening it.
> __-R__ reveal flag | __file.txt__ the target file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __-g__ flag allows you to open an application in the background without bringing it to the front. You can also use __open__ to launch URLs directly in your default web browser.

